.SH NAME
ivcap-job-events - Stream events for a job


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBivcap job events [flags] job-id\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stream job-related events in real-time. Events are displayed as they occur.
The service-id is resolved automatically from the job record in the datafabric.

.PP
Examples:
  ivcap job events urn:ivcap:job:456
  ivcap job events --max-messages 10 job-id
  ivcap job events --last-event-id abc123 job-id


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for events

.PP
\fB--last-event-id\fP=""
	Last event ID to resume from

.PP
\fB--max-messages\fP=0
	Maximum number of messages to return (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB--max-wait-time\fP=30
	Max wait time for new events in seconds


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
